description:
FILED s531a merge (the reviewing session, Opus 5.5, 2026-11-01), from the merge probe.  Strictly better than main (main crashes on this program at the call, #3831); the shapes that matter (delete in BEGIN -- namespace::clean / Role-Tiny -- and a string eval after the delete) are right.

    package Foo; sub gone { "kept" } package main;
    sub callit { Foo::gone() }
    delete $Foo::{gone};
    print callit(), " ", (defined &Foo::gone ? "def" : "undef"), "\n";
    print eval q{ defined &Foo::gone } ? "eval-def\n" : "eval-undef\n";
    BEGIN { package Bar; sub b { 1 } } BEGIN { delete $Bar::{b} }
    print defined &Bar::b ? "bar-def\n" : "bar-undef\n";

perl 5.40.3: kept def / eval-undef / bar-undef.   main 25813c08: dies "Undefined subroutine &Foo::gone called" (#3831).   s531a tree cc5f6310: kept UNDEF / eval-undef / bar-undef.

CAUSE: s531a's #3696 rule binds a literal `defined &NAME` / `exists &NAME` to its glob when its top-level FORM LOADS; perl compiles the WHOLE file before running any of it, so a run-time delete earlier in the same file has not happened yet at compile time.  Same family as the phase model across sections (#456 half (b), #469): PCL loads and runs top-level forms one at a time.  A fix would bind such literals at the unit's compile phase (the file's first form) for names already defined then -- measure the cost first; low priority (a run-time delete followed by a literal defined-test in the same file is rare; the idioms delete at BEGIN / end of scope).

Probe: scratchpad m531a/p2.pl (s531 reviewing session).
